cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Deep Reinforcement Learning for Order Execution on Hyperliquid"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Idrus
    given-names: Fardeen
repository-code: "https://github.com/FardeenIdrus/drl-optimal-order-execution"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered evaluation of deep reinforcement learning for optimal trade
  execution. The venue's own short-horizon predictability is measured from
  per-order Hyperliquid data, injected at certified strength into a calibrated
  queue-reactive simulator, and DQN and PPO agents are tested on whether they
  can convert a signal known to be present, against TWAP benchmarks under
  paired common-random-number scoring.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - optimal-execution
  - market-microstructure
  - limit-order-book
  - quantitative-finance
